{"question" "e-5518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/bfdf3147fb8488c3a0032f9dad326b5d8c3ff68be46738dc39215e5098af6272.png)\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}^3$ shown above. What is the value of $a-b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/example-5518.json" "file_sha256" "9710744f8bbecfeb966a3f9d1bf41e32e8e685a07a32b5101b7346669f8ca257"} {"question" "e-5518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/35814ac6d965ac688907d162b45d9b0b194ea40375d4e474466e4fb4b1de1c1b.png) we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8x-5y \\\\ -3x-6y \\\\ -4x+5y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5y-8x \\\\ -3x-6y \\\\ 5y-4x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/f59824c26875665fcbd8adfc5414fa7b0c60254e01f725f9ca72cf1d370a3e8b.png)\n\nFinally, $a-b=(-5)-(-4)=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/example-5518.json" "file_sha256" "9710744f8bbecfeb966a3f9d1bf41e32e8e685a07a32b5101b7346669f8ca257"} {"question" "e-5519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2,$ find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/7a6d4db6774da29f9b89996e348fad61b281737db6b44e9a39efa016fa2f15f3.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/example-5519.json" "file_sha256" "e55874261c1d28ff72df0415f6a02923b5d1a8b2fa3fc9c9864b57efaea5dad3"} {"question" "e-5519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the fact that $\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/example-5519.json" "file_sha256" "e55874261c1d28ff72df0415f6a02923b5d1a8b2fa3fc9c9864b57efaea5dad3"}] "usage" {"q-38270" [] "e-5518" [] "q-38272" [] "q-8052" [] "q-38271" [] "q-8030" [] "e-5519" [] "e-5901" []} "basis" 1859 "retractions" [[17592186088324 :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents the linear transformation $T: R^{3} → R^{2}$, where\n\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2x - y + z \\\\ x - y - z\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186088326 :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents the linear transformation $T: R^{3} → R^{2}$, where\n\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x - 3y + 8z \\\\ x + z + 2y\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186088103 :question/problem "$T = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}ay + 2x - 2z \\\\ bz - 3x + cy\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T: R^{3} → R^{2}$ shown above. What is the value of $a + b + c$?"] [17592186088104 :question/problem "$T = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -8 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}, T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-3x + y \\\\ ax - 8y \\\\ -9x + by\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T: R^{2} → R^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $a + b$?"] [17592186088102 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T: R^{2} → R^{3}$, find $T(v)$.\n\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}, v = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186087519 :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186087519 :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNotice that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186087504 :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}^3$ shown above. What is the value of $a-b$?"] [17592186087504 :question/worked-solution "Given the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}-8x - 5y \\\\ -3x - 6y \\\\ -4x + 5y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-5y - 8x \\\\ -3x - 6y \\\\ 5y - 4x\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\na-b=(-5)-(-4)=-1\n$$"] [17592186087505 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$, find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})$.\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186087505 :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT(v) &= T \\cdot v \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186085544 17592186085545 17592186085546 17592186085547 17592186085548 17592186085550 17592186085551 17592186085552 17592186085553 17592186085554 17592186085556 17592186085557 17592186085558 17592186085559 17592186085560 17592186086875 17592186086876 17592186086877 17592186086878 17592186086879 17592186086887 17592186086888 17592186086889 17592186086890 17592186086891] "immutable_fields" [[17592186085543 :answer-field/correct] [17592186085543 :answer-field/id] [17592186085543 :answer-field/key] [17592186085543 :answer-field/type] [17592186085549 :answer-field/correct] [17592186085549 :answer-field/id] [17592186085549 :answer-field/key] [17592186085549 :answer-field/type] [17592186085555 :answer-field/correct] [17592186085555 :answer-field/id] [17592186085555 :answer-field/key] [17592186085555 :answer-field/type] [17592186086874 :answer-field/correct] [17592186086874 :answer-field/id] [17592186086874 :answer-field/key] [17592186086874 :answer-field/type] [17592186086886 :answer-field/correct] [17592186086886 :answer-field/id] [17592186086886 :answer-field/key] [17592186086886 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
